WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:03.875
Dungeons and Dragons,
at first regarded

00:00:03.958 --> 00:00:05.708
as a harmless game
of make believe

00:00:05.792 --> 00:00:08.458
now has both parents
and psychologists concerned.

00:00:09.292 --> 00:00:12.458
Studies have linked violent
behaviour to the game,

00:00:12.958 --> 00:00:14.792
saying it promotes
satanic worship,

00:00:15.458 --> 00:00:21.208
ritual sacrifice,
sodomy, suicide and even…

00:00:22.208 --> 00:00:23.042
murder.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.500
This year, it's my year.

00:00:27.708 --> 00:00:28.500
I can feel it.

00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:29.750
&lt;i&gt;Do you ever feel like…&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:32.292
you're losing your mind.

00:00:33.417 --> 00:00:34.833
On a daily basis.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:37.833
I mean, I feel like
I'm losing my mind right now

00:00:37.917 --> 00:00:41.042
doing a drug deal
with Chrissy Cunningham,

00:00:41.125 --> 00:00:43.542
the Queen of Hawkins High.

00:00:53.375 --> 00:00:54.708
Welcome to hellfire.

00:00:57.542 --> 00:00:59.167
But Vecna? Man!

00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:02.667
There is no shame
in running.

00:01:07.292 --> 00:01:10.208
Peaceful bliss
just moments away.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:14.083
Chrissy?

00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:18.333
Chrissy.

00:01:19.958 --> 00:01:21.667
Hello? Hey, Chrissy.

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:24.458
Eddie.

00:01:26.458 --> 00:01:30.958
We just want to talk.

00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:35.042
I wanna know what happened.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.083
You won't believe me.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.375
Try us.

00:01:43.125 --> 00:01:48.042
&lt;i&gt;Her body just, like,&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;lifted up into the air.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:48.125 --> 00:01:49.042
&lt;i&gt;And, uh…&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.292
&lt;i&gt;She just hung there.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:54.292 --> 00:01:55.292
In the air.

00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:57.833
And her bones, uh…

00:02:00.458 --> 00:02:03.292
Her bones started to snap.

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:08.583
I didn't know what to do so,
uh, I…

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.375
I ran away.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:17.625
&lt;i&gt;He does things.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:17.708 --> 00:02:18.542
You there?

00:02:18.625 --> 00:02:20.458
It's Eddie.
You remember me, right?

00:02:20.542 --> 00:02:23.500
And we are now doing
everything in our power

00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:24.417
to find him.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:25.875
Anybody?

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.917
I say you're asking me
to follow you into Mordor.

00:02:35.042 --> 00:02:36.333
So, Mordor it is.

00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:39.167
-Steve.
-Steve.

00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:43.833
Oh, this is so stupid.

00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:44.875
This is so stupid.

00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:55.500
Outside of D&amp;D I am no hero.

00:02:55.583 --> 00:02:59.667
I see danger and
I just turn heel and run.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.000
Or at least
that's what I've learned

00:03:02.083 --> 00:03:03.792
about myself this week.

00:03:03.875 --> 00:03:05.292
Here we go again.

00:03:06.042 --> 00:03:09.250
Yes! That was fun.

00:03:09.333 --> 00:03:11.333
Light, but durable.

00:03:11.417 --> 00:03:14.000
There will be no more
retreating.

00:03:15.417 --> 00:03:16.625
What are you doing?

00:03:17.333 --> 00:03:19.958
Never change,
Dustin Henderson.

00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:23.250
Don't try to be cute or be
a hero or something, okay?

00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:24.833
-You guys are just--
-Decoys.

00:03:24.917 --> 00:03:26.875
Absolutely.
I mean, look at us.

00:03:27.875 --> 00:03:29.583
We are not heroes.

00:03:30.083 --> 00:03:31.333
Now for the fun part.

00:03:33.375 --> 00:03:35.458
Chrissy, this is for you.

00:03:48.208 --> 00:03:49.208
Game on in 20.

00:04:01.292 --> 00:04:02.667
One.

00:04:03.958 --> 00:04:05.250
Eddie.

00:04:05.333 --> 00:04:06.292
What are you doing?

00:04:06.375 --> 00:04:07.250
Eddie, no.

00:04:09.542 --> 00:04:10.875
Stop.

00:04:11.375 --> 00:04:12.917
Eddie, what are you doing?

00:04:14.625 --> 00:04:16.292
-I'm buying more time.
-No.

00:04:16.375 --> 00:04:17.458
Eddie, please.

00:04:20.792 --> 00:04:24.500
Come get me,
you sons of bitches.

00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:29.292
&lt;i&gt;I didn't know&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;what to do, so I…&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:30.708 --> 00:04:31.542
I ran away.

00:04:41.375 --> 00:04:42.458
He could have run.

00:04:43.792 --> 00:04:45.583
He could have saved himself.

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:49.917
He fought and died
to protect this town.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.250
Come on. Come on!

00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:54.208
This town that hated him.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:04:59.625
Oh God.

00:04:59.708 --> 00:05:02.417
I didn't run away this time,
right?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.042
No. No, no, no.

00:05:05.625 --> 00:05:06.458
You didn't run.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.292
He isn't just innocent.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:13.000
He's a hero.

00:05:13.083 --> 00:05:15.708
I think it's my year,
Anderson.

00:05:17.042 --> 00:05:20.375
I think
it's finally my year.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.250
&lt;i&gt;I wish everyone&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;i&gt;had gotten to know him.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:27.333 --> 00:05:28.458
&lt;i&gt;Really know him.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:31.125 --> 00:05:33.167
Because they would
have loved him.

